---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Blog" current="">
  <section class="page">
    <div class="pagehead"><h2>The Buzz columns</h2><span>Two voices, one Austin</span></div>
    <p>Local Buzz ATX explains the news. These columnists add the flavor.</p>

    <div class="pagehead" id="caleb"><h2>Caleb's Corner</h2><span>tech, business, AI and Austin growth</span></div>
    <div class="colcards"><div class="colcard">
      <img class="art-av art-av-lg" src="/authors/caleb.jpg" alt="Illustration of Caleb" width="56" height="56" />
      <div><b>Caleb</b><p>Caleb looks at where Austin is growing: startups, AI tools, big tech arrivals and what they mean for work and money. Clear, analytical and no hype.</p></div>
    </div></div>
    <p class="art-sample">The first Caleb's Corner column is coming soon.</p>

    <div class="pagehead" id="tori"><h2>Quick Tea</h2><span>entertainment, music, culture and Austin buzz</span></div>
    <div class="colcards"><div class="colcard">
      <img class="art-av art-av-lg" src="/authors/tori.jpg" alt="Illustration of Tori" width="56" height="56" />
      <div><b>Tori</b><p>Tori gives a quick, honest take on the entertainment stories people are talking about. She sticks to confirmed news and leaves rumors out.</p></div>
    </div></div>
    <p class="art-sample">The first Quick Tea is coming soon.</p>

    <p class="aitag">Caleb and Tori are pen names, and their pictures are illustrations. The columns are AI-assisted and based on public reporting, with links to the original stories. <a href="/about">About Local Buzz ATX</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
